---
title: Sources
description: External data sources used by the scraper.
section: Scraper
order: 2
---

## Spotify

Primary source for music metadata. Uses `spotify-web-api-node`.

**Data obtained:**
- Track title, duration, ISRC
- Album title, cover art, release year
- Artist name, genres
- Spotify track ID (used for deduplication)

**Authentication:** OAuth2 client credentials flow.

## YouTube

Audio source. Uses `yt-dlp-wrap` to invoke `yt-dlp`.

**Process:**
1. Search YouTube for the track (title + artist)
2. Select best match
3. Download audio stream
4. Convert to HLS segments

**Requirement:** `yt-dlp` must be installed on the system.

## Last.fm

Supplementary metadata source for artist images and additional data.

**Data obtained:**
- High-resolution artist images
- Artist bio and tags
- Similar artists

**Authentication:** API key (free registration).

## Genius

Lyrics source. Uses the `genius-lyrics` package.

**Data obtained:**
- Song lyrics (plain text)
- Multiple language variants when available

## Deezer / iTunes

Fallback sources for cover art and metadata verification. Accessed via public APIs (no authentication required).
